{
  "id": "VA-HB-1318-2015",
  "scope": "state:va",
  "title": "HB 1318 (2015 Regular Session (LIS session code 151)): Absentee ballots; photo identification required for submission of application.",
  "urls": [
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?151+sum+HB1318",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?151+mbr+HB1318",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?151+ful+HB1318ER",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?151+ful+HB1318 (introduced; not read)",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?151+ful+HB1318E (engrossed; not read)"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id)\n(section) § 24.2-701 B 2 (as passed (enrolled; struck words removed, new words kept))\n(quote) 2. Any other application may be made by mail or by electronic or telephonic transmission to a facsimile device if one is available to the office of the general registrar or the office of the State Board if a device is not available locally, or other means. The application shall be on a form furnished by the registrar, and the applicant shall submit with his application a copy of one of the forms of identification specified in subsection B of § 24.2-643. Such requirement shall not apply to a registered voter who is qualified to vote by absentee ballot pursuant to subdivision 2 or subdivision 4 of § 24.2-700. An application, if made under subdivision 2 of § 24.2-700, may be on a federal postcard application prescribed pursuant to 52 U.S.C. § 20301(b)(2). The federal postcard application may be accepted the later of (i) 12 months before an election or (ii) the day following any election held in the twelfth month prior to the election in which the applicant is applying to vote. The application shall be made to the appropriate registrar no later than 5:00 p.m. on the seventh day prior to the election in which the applicant offers to vote.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n\n(other) Only § 24.2-701 is amended; no other subject.",
  "sponsors": [
    {
      "name": "Jeffrey L. Campbell",
      "role": "author",
      "version": "Enrolled (HB1318ER, 2/25/2015); passed both chambers; vetoed by Governor 3/27/2015; veto not overridden 4/15/2015 (65-Y 34-N; 66 needed)"
    }
  ],
